			<div class="content" id="post-content-2775190">
									

<blockquote>
<p><em>We die in the darkness, so that you may live in the light&#8230; Yeah, right!</em></p>
</blockquote>
<p>This is my SCP-3000 proposal for this contest.</p>
<p>Firstly, allow me to express thanks to various reviewers like Gog33, Dr-Prentice, Bluemorpho, GibberingEloquence, LordStonefish, Targellon. Triple thanks to both psul and Petrograd, who took the trouble of looking at it thrice.</p>
<p>Image by Tormod Sandtrov of Flickr (<a href="https://www.flickr.com/photos/tormods/3841034148">https://www.flickr.com/photos/tormods/3841034148</a>) under CC BY-SA 2.0; changes made include the addition of blackboxes</p>
<p>This article also involves the following:</p>
<ul>
<li>Church of the Broken God hub by FortuneFavorsBold</li>
<li>SCP-428 (The Crowd) by DrScooter</li>
<li>SCP-343 (&quot;God&quot;) by Unknown Author</li>
<li>I Thought You Died Alone by A Random Day</li>
</ul>
<p>And as for spoilers,</p>
<div class="collapsible-block">
<div class="collapsible-block-folded"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">+&nbsp;show&nbsp;block</a></div>
<div class="collapsible-block-unfolded" style="display:none">
<div class="collapsible-block-unfolded-link"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">–&nbsp;hide&nbsp;block</a></div>
<div class="collapsible-block-content">
<p>The Foundation's position re: the instances is that they are Foundation members who died violently in-line of duty. Keyword is &quot;Foundation's position&quot;, i.e. not the reality of it.</p>
<p>The instances definitely remember how they die, and that becomes their trauma even into their next lives.</p>
<p>Also, check the death date for -5 and birth date for -48. It's in dd/mm/yyyy formatting.</p>
</div>
</div>
</div>

